# The build only needs requirements.txt, the two .py files, and web/. Everything else
# is either rebuilt inside the image or must never enter it.

# Secrets. Nothing here is COPYed, but a build context is not a private place - anything
# in it is one careless `COPY . .` away from being in a layer forever.
.env
token.json
*.pem

# Rebuilt in the image: pip installs from requirements.txt, npm ci from package-lock.json,
# and Vite writes dist/ in the web stage. Copying the host's copies in would be slower and
# would carry Windows-built artifacts into a Linux image.
venv/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Not code.
.git/
.gitignore
.claude/
README.md
ROADMAP.md
check_auth.py
check_tools.py
